","us":"pʊt ɑːn","uk":"pʊt ɒn"},{"id":26,"w":"take off","tr":"çıkarmak; havalanmak","def":"to remove clothes; (a plane) to leave the ground","ex":"The plane [took off] on time.","type":"s","us":"teɪk ɔːf","uk":"teɪk ɒf"},{"id":27,"w":"turn on","tr":"açmak (cihaz)","def":"to start a machine","ex":"[Turn on] the lights.","type":"s","us":"tɝːn ɑːn","uk":"tɜːn ɒn"},{"id":28,"w":"turn off","tr":"kapatmak (cihaz)","def":"to stop a machine","ex":"[Turn off] your phone.","type":"s","us":"tɝːn ɔːf","uk":"tɜːn ɒf"},{"id":29,"w":"turn down","tr":"reddetmek; kısmak","def":"to refuse; to lower the volume","ex":"She [turned down] the job offer.","type":"s","us":"tɝːn daʊn","uk":"tɜːn daʊn"},{"id":30,"w":"turn up","tr":"gelmek; açmak (ses)","def":"to arrive; to increase the volume","ex":"He [turned up] late again.","type":"s","us":"tɝːn ʌp","uk":"tɜːn ʌp"},{"id":31,"w":"work out","tr":"spor yapmak; çözmek; yolunda gitmek","def":"to exercise; to solve; to end well","ex":"I [work out] three times a week.","type":"s","us":"wɝːk aʊt","uk":"wɜːk aʊt"},{"id":32,"w":"figure out","tr":"çözmek; anlamak","def":"to understand after thinking","ex":"I can't [figure out] this problem.","type":"s","us":"ˈfɪɡjɚ aʊt","uk":"ˈfɪɡə aʊt"},{"id":33,"w":"come on","tr":"hadi; açılmak","def":"used to encourage; to start working","ex":"[Come on], we're late!","type":"n","us":"kʌm ɑːn","uk":"kʌm ɒn"},{"id":34,"w":"go off","tr":"çalmak (alarm); patlamak; bozulmak","def":"to ring; to explode; (food) to go bad","ex":"My alarm [went off] at six.","type":"n","us":"ɡoʊ ɔːf","uk":"ɡəʊ ɒf"},{"id":35,"w":"end up","tr":"sonunda ... olmak","def":"to finally be in a place or situation","ex":"We [ended up] staying at home.","type":"n","us":"ɛnd ʌp","uk":"end ʌp"},{"id":36,"w":"bring up","tr":"gündeme getirmek; yetiştirmek","def":"to mention; to raise a child","ex":"She [brought up] three children alone.","type":"s","us":"brɪŋ ʌp","uk":"brɪŋ ʌp"},{"id":37,"w":"break down","tr":"bozulmak; yıkılmak","def":"to stop working;